-- title:
--   Eq. (46): $\tau_B\circ\pi=\tau_A$ on $\mathcal F^A_t$ iff $t<d_{\mathrm{rel}}$
-- statement:
--   Let $H_A=\mathbb C^{N_A}$ and $H_B=\mathbb C^{N_B}$ be finite-dimensional Hilbert spaces, let $a_1,\dots,a_s$ be operators on $H_A$ and $b_1,\dots,b_s$ operators on $H_B$ (no further assumption on them), and let $\mathcal A=C^*(I_A,a_1,\dots,a_s)$ be the unital $*$-algebra they generate. Let $\pi:\mathcal A\to B(H_B)$ be a unital $*$-homomorphism with $\pi(a_i)=b_i$. Write $\tau_L(X)=\operatorname{Tr}X/N_L$ for the normalized trace, $\|X\|_{2,L}=\sqrt{\tau_L(X^*X)}$, $\mathcal F^A_t$ for the span of the identity and of all marked words $a_{i_1}^{\epsilon_1}\cdots a_{i_\ell}^{\epsilon_\ell}$ with $\ell\le t$ and $\epsilon_j\in\{1,*\}$, and $d_{\mathrm{rel}}\in\mathbb N_0\cup\{+\infty\}$ for the relative distance (Definition 4.1).
--
--   Then for every integer $t\ge0$,
--
--   $$\tau_B\circ\pi=\tau_A\ \text{on}\ \mathcal F^A_t\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad t<d_{\mathrm{rel}}.$$
--
--   This is the threshold reading of the relative distance: the traces agree on every degree space below $d_{\mathrm{rel}}$ and on none from $d_{\mathrm{rel}}$ on. Both directions of Proposition 4.2 pass through it.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: Hilbert spaces H_A, H_B with N_L = dim H_L ≥ 1 (τ_L divides by N_L) → index types nA, nB may be empty, where Lean's x/0 = 0 gives τ_L ≡ 0; reason: covers only extra degenerate instances where the source's τ_L is undefined; on nonempty index types it is the source's statement verbatim
--   - encoding: A = C∗(I_A, a₁,…,a_s) ⊆ B(H_A), π : A ↠ B unital ∗-homomorphism with π(aᵢ) = bᵢ → A = StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range a) in Matrix nA nA ℂ; π : A →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix nB nB ℂ with π (gen a i) = b i; reason: in finite dimension the generated ∗-subalgebra is norm closed (App. E, p.85); the range of π is the ∗-subalgebra generated by the bᵢ, i.e. B, so 'onto B' is automatic
--   - encoding: marked words a_{i₁}^{ϵ₁}⋯a_{i_ℓ}^{ϵ_ℓ}, ϵⱼ ∈ {1, ∗}, empty word = I_A; 𝓕ᴬ_t their span for ℓ ≤ t → words are List (Fin s × Bool) with true = adjoint, evaluated by wordEval; 𝓕ᴬ_t = markedSpace a t, a Submodule ℂ of A; reason: Lean convention; same spaces
--   - encoding: d_rel ∈ ℕ₀ ∪ {+∞}, empty minimum +∞ → relDist a π : ℕ∞ as sInf of the image in ℕ∞, sInf ∅ = ⊤; reason: Lean convention; same values
-- source:
--   Shang, Stilck França, From Simple Sources to Quantum Advantage: Homomorphic Polynomial Transduction via Relative Decoding, arXiv:2609.35101 (held version, sha256 d2be7859…), Definition 4.1, eq. (46), p.18 (pdf_page 18)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_LIDT_MIPStarRE_Quantum_FiniteMatrix_NormalizedTrace
import Definitions.Def_RelDecoding_markedSpace
import Definitions.Def_RelDecoding_relDist

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace RelDecoding

open LIDT.MIPStarRE.Quantum

/-- **Eq. (46), threshold reading of the relative distance.** For every integer `t ≥ 0`,
`τ_B ∘ π = τ_A` on `𝓕ᴬ_t` if and only if `t < d_rel`. Shang, Stilck França, *From Simple
Sources to Quantum Advantage: Homomorphic Polynomial Transduction via Relative Decoding*,
arXiv:2609.35101 (held version, sha256 d2be7859…), Definition 4.1, eq. (46), p.18.

**Formalization Note.** `A = C∗(I_A, a)` is `StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range a)` in
`Matrix nA nA ℂ`; `π` is a unital ∗-homomorphism from `A` into `Matrix nB nB ℂ` with
`π(aᵢ) = bᵢ`; `τ_L = Tr / N_L`; `d_rel ∈ ℕ∞` with `+∞` for the empty minimum. The index types
may be empty (then `τ ≡ 0` by Lean's `x / 0 = 0`). -/
theorem eq_46 {nA nB : Type*} [Fintype nA] [DecidableEq nA] [Fintype nB] [DecidableEq nB]
    {s : ℕ} (a : Fin s → Matrix nA nA ℂ) (b : Fin s → Matrix nB nB ℂ)
    (π : genAlg a →⋆ₐ[ℂ] Matrix nB nB ℂ) (hπ : ∀ i, π (gen a i) = b i) (t : ℕ) :
    (∀ Y ∈ markedSpace a t, normalizedTrace (π Y) = normalizedTrace (Y : Matrix nA nA ℂ)) ↔
      (t : ℕ∞) < relDist a π := by sorry

end RelDecoding
